From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ats0c <ats0c@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 06:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] media: vb2: call poll_wait() before the early returns

vb2_core_poll() returns EPOLLERR for a queue that is not streaming (or a
capture queue still waiting for its first buffer) before it calls
poll_wait().  An epoll item registered at that point is never added to the
queue's done_wq, so no later vb2_buffer_done() wakes it.

The Exynos Codec2 components register the MFC fd with epoll during init,
before STREAMON, and then wait forever for decoded frames.  Register on
done_wq right after the direction checks, as upstream does, and drop the
later conditional poll_wait().
---
diff --git a/drivers/media/common/videobuf2/videobuf2-core.c b/drivers/media/common/videobuf2/videobuf2-core.c
index 02cd927a5d2c..29ac7958de57 100644
--- a/drivers/media/common/videobuf2/videobuf2-core.c
+++ b/drivers/media/common/videobuf2/videobuf2-core.c
@@ -2371,6 +2371,13 @@ __poll_t vb2_core_poll(struct vb2_queue *q, struct file *file,
 	if (q->is_output && !(req_events & (EPOLLOUT | EPOLLWRNORM)))
 		return 0;
 
+	/*
+	 * Register on the done queue before any early return.  An epoll item
+	 * added while the queue is not streaming yet (or is still waiting for its
+	 * first buffer) would otherwise never be woken by vb2_buffer_done().
+	 */
+	poll_wait(file, &q->done_wq, wait);
+
 	/*
 	 * Start file I/O emulator only if streaming API has not been used yet.
 	 */
@@ -2422,8 +2429,6 @@ __poll_t vb2_core_poll(struct vb2_queue *q, struct file *file,
 		 */
 		if (q->last_buffer_dequeued)
 			return EPOLLIN | EPOLLRDNORM;
-
-		poll_wait(file, &q->done_wq, wait);
 	}
 
 	/*
